#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304963 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166931 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c81626a0-6613-5f5d-9dda-df853958c571" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of a Laplace Transformed Initial Value Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16626aab-41b1-50e7-9c88-6b61819c1efb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5s+17}{(s+3)(s-1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302601}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "16626aab-41b1-50e7-9c88-6b61819c1efb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5s+17}{(s+3)(s-1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302601} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d139cec-a218-57e3-8994-0875af73f1e4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304371} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65d0344f-96cb-5c9d-88a4-f4a5b51f28ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{s+3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303072}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "65d0344f-96cb-5c9d-88a4-f4a5b51f28ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{s+3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303072} :answer-field/id #uuid "725a473b-f555-5f6a-b695-caf9bb79a521" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304389}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "daf5c29f-5732-5955-b4c0-e9cfb924874e" :question/math-academy-id "q-331940" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-3{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=$ {{field-1}},\n$\\,{X}_{2}(s)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}L{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)}=L{-3{x}_{1}(t)} \\\\ L{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)}=L{2{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}sL{{x}_{1}(t)}-{x}_{1}(0)=-3L{{x}_{1}(t)} \\\\ sL{{x}_{2}(t)}-{x}_{2}(0)=2L{{x}_{1}(t)}+L{{x}_{2}(t)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-1=-3{X}_{1}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-5=2{X}_{1}(s)+{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}.$\n\nNow, solving the first equation for ${X}_{1}(s),$ we get\n\n$$\ns{X}_{1}(s)-1=-3{X}_{1}(s)\\,⟹\\,{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{1}{s+3}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the second equation and solving for ${X}_{2}(s),$ we have\n\n$$\ns{X}_{2}(s)-5=2(\\frac{1}{s+3})+{X}_{2}(s)\\,⟹\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{5s+17}{(s+3)(s-1)}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305035 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166932 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bb88b85b-efa1-56db-8655-4b49703dda6a" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Initial Value Problem Given the Laplace Transformed Solution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "61cae97e-e1cf-5e1a-b4b8-212a90585bf0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303052}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "61cae97e-e1cf-5e1a-b4b8-212a90585bf0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303052} :answer-field/id #uuid "134108ac-f6ce-5da7-ad51-84bc71a18543" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304117} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "af54400f-b9f6-5982-9407-f85ff881920b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303536}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "af54400f-b9f6-5982-9407-f85ff881920b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303536} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d5e1211-c6d7-5e87-9299-f69543b35e89" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304373} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3cbd3de9-8819-58ec-a936-9fa202688522" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302832}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3cbd3de9-8819-58ec-a936-9fa202688522" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302832} :answer-field/id #uuid "bbc227f3-81a3-5cb5-bb5e-0ade1394f95f" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304588} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eb0ca108-a376-5088-a942-5cb1c1a219af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303925}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eb0ca108-a376-5088-a942-5cb1c1a219af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303925} :answer-field/id #uuid "eee805e2-49aa-5088-bab0-02cbf6bbb3dc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304722}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7ac0cd29-2f59-5bca-b5ae-84aff2ab783d" :question/math-academy-id "q-332409" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-3{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution\n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}=\\frac{1}{2s}+\\frac{7}{2(s-4)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}=\\frac{3}{2s}-\\frac{7}{2(s-4)}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n| $x(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  | $\\,\\,+\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  | $\\,\\,{e}^{4t}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} |  |  | {{field-4}} |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{1}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{2s}+\\frac{7}{2(s-4)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}}+\\frac{7}{2}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 1+\\frac{7}{2}{e}^{4\\cdot t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{7}{2}{e}^{4t} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{2}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{3}{2s}-\\frac{7}{2(s-4)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}}-\\frac{7}{2}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot 1-\\frac{7}{2}{e}^{4\\cdot t} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}-\\frac{7}{2}{e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\nx(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{7}{2}{e}^{4t} \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}-\\frac{7}{2}{e}^{4t}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{7}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{7}{2}\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{4t}.\n$$"}]}
